# Sakura: petals fall, land and make notes by themselves; the keys shake the blossoms and blow gusts; the
# knobs move activity, time, tone and space; the style switches; nothing grows without bound
# (ZEN-1 boots into the scene)
wait 800
wait 50
expect mode 1
wait 3000
shot sakura-start.png
wait 27000
expect landed >5
# (a note or more in the first half minute: how many depends on the seed's first gusts)
expect scnotes >0
expect peak_db_max <-6
shot sakura-30s.png
# the default is unhurried: over two minutes, a landing note every three or four seconds,
# most of them echoed once, softly. Across ten seeds: 33..52 landing notes in two minutes (gusts' runs
# count too); this boot's seed is a busy one (~58)
wait 90000
expect scnotes >18
expect scnotes <65
expect echoes >8
expect echoes <45
expect drones >0
# a busy minute at full activity and double speed stays a few notes a second at most
spin K2 30
wait 60000
expect scnotes <400
expect nvoices <13
# a full engine never takes the drone's two voices
expect drones >0
shot sakura-busy.png
tapkey w3
tapkey b8
wait 5000
shot sakura-gust.png
spin K3 2
spin K4 -10
wait 300
shot sakura-knobs.png
tap GLO
wait 2000
expect style 1
shot sakura-pixel.png
# keys. A white key plays its note at once (sixteen notes, each its own, rising from 3: w0 -> 3, w13 -> 16); a black key plays
# the harp, its own note, low to high (b0 -> 3, b9 -> 12)
tapkey w7
wait 20
expect keynote 10
tapkey w0
wait 20
expect keynote 3
tapkey w13
wait 20
expect keynote 16
tapkey b0
wait 20
expect keynote 3
tapkey b9
wait 20
expect keynote 12
expect harpkeys >1
# the night (yozakura: the tree lit, lanterns, their light on the river): drawn and sent whole
dayat 0.7
wait 4000
shot night.png
expect stale 0
expect race 0
press HOME
wait 800
release HOME
wait 6000
expect mode 0
expect nvoices 0
# only what changed is sent to the screen; the screen as sent always matches the frame as drawn
expect stale 0
expect race 0
